<%#
  The layout of every page a visitor sees: published pages, the 404 page,
  the draft preview, and what a sent form is answered with (a confirmation,
  a refusal, or the page drawn again above the list of what to put right,
  @form_errors). No csrf_meta_tags and no csp_meta_tag: either
  would read the session, and a session writes a cookie onto a page meant
  to be cached and shared. No script either; the Content-Security-Policy
  (PublicPage) says script-src 'none'. The header and footer are the
  site's parts (SiteParts), drawn from blocks as the page is: each its
  published version, or its starter until it has one, the same on every
  page; the preview draws their drafts. A part with no section draws
  nothing. The main content's id has an underscore, which a section anchor
  cannot hold (the schema's ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$), so no anchor can take
  the skip link's target.
-%>
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title><%= @title %></title>
<%= tag.meta(name: "description", content: @description) if @description.present? %>
<%= tag.meta(name: "robots", content: "noindex") if @noindex %>
<%= tag.link(rel: "icon", href: image_path("site-mark.svg"), type: "image/svg+xml") %>
<%= preload_link_tag("archivo-variable.woff2") %>
<%= preload_link_tag("source-serif-4-variable.woff2") %>
<%= stylesheet_link_tag("site", "tokens") %>
</head>
<body>
<%= tag.div(class: "site", data: site_style_data(site_style)) do %><div class="sw">
<a class="sw-skip" href="#main_content">Skip to content</a>
<%= site_part(site_parts.fetch("header"), :header) %>
<main id="main_content">
<%= render("pages/form_errors", errors: @form_errors) if @form_errors -%>
<%= yield %>
</main>
<%= site_part(site_parts.fetch("footer"), :footer) %>
</div><% end %>
</body>
</html>
